KWin: lone frames aimed at the next vblank (KWIN_LONE_FRAME_LEAD_US; 6.7.5 port of patches/kwin/0039, 2026-10-26)

For vitrine's 6.7.5 guest series (its 1.27.2: Patch100-127; after kwin-frame-slack-precise-timer, which turns the
composite timer into compositeTimerActive(), and kwin-early-lone-frames). A lone frame - the first after an idle
stretch: no frame in flight, none presented for two refreshes or more, the composite timer not armed - is aimed at
the next vblank when that is at least the lead away, else at the one after, and rendered at once, skipping the render
estimate + safety margin + slack and the triple-buffering hysteresis. Without it a nested KWin planned every key's frame
two refreshes ahead (estimate 2 ms composited + host deadline + 1 ms + slack ~ 4.1 ms >= 95 % of 4.17 ms at 240 Hz).
Measured on 6.7.91 in the nested desktop (2026-10-09): the minimal client's key -> screen 9.4-9.5 ms against 11.0
(bare metal 9.3-9.4), no more "slow" sessions; ~3 extra repeats in 52 launcher animations with the host GPU 40 % busy.
Port: 6.7.5 has one pageflipsSince (counted from now: 6.7.91 split it into pageflipsSince and pageflipsSinceNow;
this uses it for both) and compositeTimerActive() instead of compositeTimer.isActive(). Needs none of the host's
lone-frame patches (0021-0025 / 0074). Applies with fuzz 0 after Patch127; not built or run here.
Unset: off. Research's nested session sets KWIN_LONE_FRAME_LEAD_US=2500, 1500 on an Intel xe host.

