+// KWIN_LONE_FRAME_LEAD_US (EXP): how close to the next vblank a lone frame - the first after an
+// idle stretch (no frame in flight, none presented for two refreshes or more) - may still be
+// aimed at it: at least this far off, the next vblank, else the one after; rendered at once,
+// without the render estimate + safety margin + slack and the triple-buffering hysteresis. A
+// nested compositor's margin covers a busy host (its reported deadline + 1 ms) and the estimate
+// counts a composited frame as 2 ms: ~4.1-6 ms before the vblank at 240 Hz, so every lone frame -
+// a key's - went two refreshes ahead. The host takes a lone commit ~2.2 ms before its vblank
+// (2026-10-09, research/guest-client-overhead-2026-10-09.md); a frame that misses is shown a
+// refresh later through commit timing, where it lands anyway, and with nothing in flight there is
+// no frame cadence for the hysteresis to protect. Unset: off.
+static const std::optional<std::chrono::nanoseconds> s_loneFrameLead = qEnvironmentVariableIsEmpty("KWIN_LONE_FRAME_LEAD_US")
+    ? std::nullopt
+    : std::optional<std::chrono::nanoseconds>(std::chrono::microseconds(std::max(0, qEnvironmentVariableIntValue("KWIN_LONE_FRAME_LEAD_US"))));
 
